EXT. FROZEN LAKE LANDSDAL - BONSPIEL RINK - DAY

A white plain under a lower white sky. Eight sheets of curling ice scraped clean. Flags snapping. Crowds in wool, breath rising.

At the far house, ASTRID NYGAARD, 30s, skip, tall, ice in her braid, crouches behind the button, broom raised. Her three teammates wait down the sheet: TORVALD, 50s, burly, thick gloves; INGE, 20s, whip-thin, the lead; and HALVOR, 60s, slow-moving, the veteran.

At the hack, LINNEA, 20s, her youngest sweeper, adjusts her grip on a stone.

The score reads 6-6. Final end.

ASTRID
(calling)
Linnea! Heavy! Heavy!

LINNEA
Heavy?

ASTRID
Draw to the button. One more.

LINNEA
Right.

Linnea pushes off. Slides. The stone glides. A hush spreads. Even the wind seems to listen.

TORVALD
Left, Inge! Sweep!

INGE
I am sweeping!

HALVOR
Harder!

TORVALD
Harder!

INGE
Harder than hard!

The stone creeps down the ice. Their brooms hiss. It curls toward the house -- and stops, a hair short.

Groans from the crowd. Astrid hangs her head.

TORVALD
Short.

HALVOR
Short by a hair.

INGE
That was my sweeping.

TORVALD
It wasn't you.

HALVOR
It was the ice.

ASTRID
It was me.

A heavy silence. Down the sheet, the other team's final stone is already gliding home. It is perfect. It hits the button. The crowd cheers.

A whistle. REFEREE ODDMUND, 60s, in a parka marked OFFICIAL, strides out across the ice with a measuring tape, grim as a judge.

ODDMUND
Measurement! Measurement on the stones!

The crowd falls quiet. Oddmund kneels. Unrolls the tape. Measures. Measures again.

ODDMUND (CONT'D)
(looking up)
Nygaard stone. Four centimeters. Their stone. Four-point-one.

INGE
We won?

TORVALD
We won!

HALVOR
We won by a tenth!

LINNEA
By a tenth of what?

HALVOR
Of anything!

ASTRID
(breathless)
Oddmund. Measure again.

ODDMUND
I've measured twice.

ASTRID
Then measure again.

Oddmund sighs, kneels, measures a third time. The crowd leans in. Wind turns the flags.

ODDMUND
(softly)
Four-point-one. Four-point-one. Nygaard stone, four.

A beat. Then the roar goes up. Torvald lifts Astrid off the ice. Halvor sits down on his broom. Inge dances. Linnea stares at her own gloves.

ASTRID
(to Linnea)
You pushed it.

LINNEA
It stopped short.

ASTRID
It was exactly enough.

Down the sheet, the other team's stones sit silent on the ice. Wind drifts snow across them.

TORVALD
They threw a perfect last stone.

HALVOR
Not perfect enough.

ASTRID
Then they'll be back.
